// N114: fused gated delta-net (GDN) DECODE kernels for Intel Xe2 (Arc Pro B70) as a torch XPU op library
// (torch.ops.n114gdn.*). Replaces SGLang's per-layer GDN decode tail for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (36 linear-attention layers,
// 16 key heads / 48 value heads of 128):
//
//   today (SGLang 0.5.20 on XPU, num_v_heads / num_k_heads = 3 -> fix_query_key_value_ordering branch):
//     b.contiguous, a.contiguous, cat(q, k, v)       3 copy kernels
//     causal_conv1d_update (Triton)                  1
//     fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule_packed_decode 1 (l2norm q/k, gates, recurrence)
//     z reshape copy (bs > 1), RMSNormGated (Triton) 1-2
//   here:
//     conv:     depthwise causal conv (width 4) + conv-state shift + silu, read straight from the in_proj_qkvz output
//               (the first q_dim + k_dim + v_dim columns ARE the concatenated q | k | v), written as bf16 [B, C]
//     rec_norm: one work-group per (row, value head): q / k l2 norms, softplus / sigmoid gates from the raw in_proj_ba
//               output (b | a columns), FP32 recurrence on the [V, K] state slice held in registers, bf16 rounding of o
//               exactly where SGLang stores it, then the gated RMS norm (norm_before_gate, sigmoid or silu gate) over the
//               head's 128 outputs and the bf16 output row ready for out_proj.  Optionally (ba != null) the alpha / beta
//               projection itself (two 2560-long dot products per head, Strata's fused_gdn_ab) so the in_proj_ba GEMM
//               disappears too.
//
// Port of Strata's fused_gdn_conv_l2 / fused_gdn_ab / fused_gdn_step_norm (sycl/src/kernels/cuda/fused_gdn.dp.cpp of
// github.com/Niko1221/Strata, HEAD 82f46a8), adapted to SGLang's layouts and rounding points:
//   * state pool [slots, H, V, K] (fp32 or bf16), value row v of head h contiguous over k (Strata: [k][h][v]); a thread
//     owns RPT = 128 / RG consecutive k entries of one value column, the RG lanes of a column are adjacent lanes of one
//     sub-group, so the k reductions are sub-group shuffles (no shared local memory, no barrier in the recurrence);
//   * batched rows with per-row state slots (slot < 0 = padded row: output 0, no state / conv-state write);
//   * GQA head map hk = h / (H / Hk) (SGLang), not Strata's h % Hk;
//   * conv: products rounded to bf16 before the fp32 accumulation like the Triton kernel's bf16 x bf16 multiply
//     (round_prod=1, default) and the conv state in SGLang's (slots, dim, state_len) view with arbitrary strides;
//   * gates as fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule_packed_decode: g = -exp(A_log) * softplus(a + dt_bias) (threshold 20),
//     beta = bf16(sigmoid(b)); q, k l2-normalised elementwise (x / sqrt(sum x^2 + 1e-6)), q * scale; state decayed
//     first, then kv = S.k, v' = (v - kv) * beta, S += k v', o = S.q;  o rounded to bf16 (SGLang's out tensor), then
//     the gated norm on that bf16 value: y = ((o * rsqrt(mean(o^2) + eps)) * w) * gate(z).
// No host synchronisation, no host reads of device data, outputs allocated with at::empty on the input's device:
// capturable in an XPU graph (the decode path runs from graph replay).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Portions derived from Strata:
//
